THIS LICENSE AGREEMENT ("Agreement") is entered into as of the Issue Date
hereof between VaultBank AG, a corporation organized and existing under the
laws of the Swiss Confederation, with its principal office at
Bahnhofstrasse 69, 8001 Zurich, Switzerland ("Licensor"), having its
subsidiary entities in the United States of America, the United Arab Emirates,
the United Kingdom of Great Britain and Northern Ireland, and the Republic of
Singapore, and the individual or legal entity ("Licensee") accessing the
VaultBank software and all associated documentation and materials.

BY ACCESSING, USING, OR DISTRIBUTING THE VAULTBANK SOFTWARE, LICENSEE AGREES
TO BE BOUND BY THE TERMS AND CONDITIONS OF THIS AGREEMENT. IF LICENSEE DOES NOT
AGREE TO THESE TERMS, DO NOT ACCESS OR USE THE SOFTWARE IN ANY MANNER.

================================================================================
1. DEFINITIONS AND INTERPRETATION
================================================================================

1.1  "Software" means the VaultBank proprietary software platform, including
     all source code, object code, binaries, documentation, configuration
     files, databases, APIs, and associated materials (collectively, the
     "VaultBank Platform"), whether in human-readable or machine-readable
     form, including any modifications, updates, patches, or enhancements
     thereto created by Licensor or its authorized agents.

1.2  "Financial Services" means any service related to deposit accounts,
     wealth management, private banking, asset custody, investment advisory,
     payment processing, credit facilities, currency exchange, or any other
     activity regulated under applicable banking and financial services laws.

1.3  "Regulated Jurisdictions" means Switzerland, United States of America,
     United Arab Emirates, United Kingdom, Singapore, European Union member
     states, Cayman Islands, British Virgin Islands, Hong Kong SAR, and any
     other jurisdiction in which VaultBank maintains a licensed financial
     services presence.

1.4  "Confidential Information" includes all non-public information
     disclosed by Licensor, including but not limited to source code,
     algorithms, trading strategies, customer data, transaction records,
     risk models, and proprietary business methods.

1.5  The headings in this Agreement are for convenience only and shall not
     affect its interpretation.

The terms of this Agreement shall be interpreted in accordance with Swiss
substantive law, with due consideration of applicable regulations in all
Regulated Jurisdictions where the Software operates.

================================================================================
2. GRANT OF LICENCE
================================================================================

2.1  Subject to the terms and conditions of this Agreement, Licensor hereby
     grants to Licensee a limited, non-exclusive, non-transferable,
     non-sublicensable, revocable licence to use the Software solely for
     internal evaluation, testing, and demonstration purposes within the
     Licensee's organisation ("Authorised Use").

2.2  The Software contains proprietary algorithms, trading systems, risk
     management frameworks, and cryptographic security protocols developed
     in accordance with:

     (a) The Swiss Banking Act of 1934 (SR 952.21) and the Swiss Banking
         Ordinance on Commercial Risk Management (SR 952.211);
     (b) The Basel III Capital Accord as implemented by the Swiss Federal
         Council and the Swiss Financial Market Supervisory Authority
         (FINMA);
     (c) Directive (EU) 2015/2366 (PSD2) and Regulation (EU) 2016/679 (GDPR);
     (d) The United States Federal Reserve Act, the Dodd-Frank Wall Street
         Reform and Consumer Protection Act of 2010, 12 CFR Part 217
         (Basel III), USA PATRIOT Act, and Bank Secrecy Act (BSA);
     (e) UAE Central Bank Regulations, the UAE Anti-Money Laundering Law
         (Federal Decree-Law No. 20 of 2018), and the Emirates Securities
         and Commodities Authority (ESCA) regulations;
     (f) The UK Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 (FSMA) and the
         Prudential Regulation Authority (PRA) Rulebook;
     (g) The Monetary Authority of Singapore (MAS) Notice 626 on Technology
         Risk Management and the Securities and Futures Act (Cap. 289);
     (h) SWIFT Customer Security Programme (CSP) standards and the
         associated security controls framework;
     (i) The Payment Card Industry Data Security Standard (PCI DSS) Version
         4.0 and all subsequent revisions;
     (j) The Wolfsberg Group Recommendations on Anti-Money Laundering
         and Counter-Terrorist Financing; and
     (k) All applicable national and supranational financial services,
         data protection, cybersecurity, and consumer protection laws.

2.3  Licensee acknowledges that the Software is designed to meet the highest
     standards of financial institution-grade security, compliance, and
     operational resilience as required by the aforementioned regulatory
     frameworks.

