3. RESTRICTIONS
================================================================================

3.1  Licensee shall NOT:

     (a) Use the Software for any commercial purpose, production
         deployment, or live financial transaction processing without
         obtaining a separate commercial banking licence from VaultBank AG;
     (b) Reverse engineer, decompile, disassemble, or attempt to derive
         the source code, algorithms, or cryptographic methods of the
         Software, except as expressly permitted under Article 6 of the
         Swiss Copyright Act or equivalent fair use provisions;
     (c) Remove, alter, or obscure any proprietary notices, copyright
         marks, trade secrets, or legends contained in the Software;
     (d) Transfer, sublicense, lease, rent, lend, or otherwise distribute
         the Software to third parties without the prior written consent
         of a VaultBank AG authorised signatory;
     (e) Use the Software in any jurisdiction where such use would
         constitute a violation of local banking secrecy laws, financial
         services regulations, or cross-border data transfer restrictions;
     (f) Employ the Software for any activity that would subject the
         Licensee to regulation under the USA PATRIOT Act, BSA/AML
         requirements, or comparable anti-money laundering legislation
         without maintaining a fully compliant BSA/AML programme;
     (g) Attempt to gain unauthorised access to any VaultBank production
         environment, customer data repository, or payment processing
         system through the use of the Software; or
     (h) Use the Software to facilitate, enable, or conceal any
         illicit financial activity, including but not limited to money
         laundering, terrorist financing, sanctions evasion, or tax
         evasion.

3.2  Licensee represents and warrants that it is not a prohibited person
     or entity under the U.S. Treasury Department's Office of Foreign
     Assets Control (OFAC) sanctions lists, the EU Consolidated List of
     Sanctions, the UAE Ministry of Foreign Affairs sanctions regime, or
     any other applicable sanctions authority, and that its use of the
     Software shall comply with all applicable export control laws
     including but not limited to the U.S. Export Administration
     Regulations (EAR) and International Traffic in Arms Regulations (ITAR).

