================================================================================
5. COMPLIANCE OBLIGATIONS
================================================================================

5.1  Licensee acknowledges that any use of the Software involves the
     processing of personal data and agrees to comply with all applicable
     data protection laws, including:

     - GDPR (Regulation (EU) 2016/679) where applicable within the EEA
       and to the processing of data of EEA data subjects globally;
     - UK GDPR (UK General Data Protection Regulation) as supplemented
       by the Data Protection Act 2018;
     - CCPA/CPRA (California Consumer Privacy Act / California Privacy
       Rights Act) where applicable to California residents;
     - UAE Federal Decree-Law No. 46 of 2021 on the Protection of Personal
       Data ("UAE Data Protection Law");
     - Swiss Federal Act on Data Protection (FADP), as revised effective
       September 1, 2023;
     - Singapore Personal Data Protection Act 2012 (PDPA);
     - The Hong Kong Personal Data (Privacy) Ordinance (Cap. 486);
     - Brazilian Lei Geral de Proteção de Dados (LGPD); and
     - Any other applicable national, regional, or local data protection
       laws.

5.2  Licensee shall implement appropriate technical and organisational
     measures in accordance with Article 32 of the GDPR and equivalent
     provisions in other applicable jurisdictions to ensure a level of
     security appropriate to the risk, including:

     (a) Pseudonymisation and encryption of personal data (AES-256 or
         equivalent industry-standard encryption);
     (b) Ensuring ongoing confidentiality, integrity, availability, and
         resilience of processing systems and services;
     (c) A process for regularly testing, assessing, and evaluating the
         effectiveness of technical and organisational measures for
         ensuring the security of the processing; and
     (d) Compliance with ISO/IEC 27001:2022, NIST Cybersecurity Framework
         (CSF) 2.0, and the CIS Controls Version 8.0.

5.3  Licensee shall cooperate fully with VaultBank AG's compliance,
     risk, and audit functions in the event of any data protection
     incident or suspected breach and shall notify VaultBank AG within
     seventy-two (72) hours of becoming aware of any such incident,
     in accordance with Article 33 of the GDPR and equivalent
     notification requirements in other jurisdictions.

5.4  The Software is designed to support compliance with the
     anti-money laundering and counter-terrorist financing obligations
     set forth in:

     - The 40 Recommendations of the Financial Action Task Force (FATF);
     - FATF Recommendation 15 (New Technologies) and the associated
       Guidance on Virtual Assets and Virtual Asset Service Providers;
     - The EU Anti-Money Laundering Directives (5AMLD and 6AMLD);
     - The U.S. Bank Secrecy Act and USA PATRIOT Act;
     - The UAE AML/CFT Framework (Federal Decree-Law No. 20 of 2018
       and Cabinet Resolution No. 58 of 2020);
     - The UK Money Laundering, Terrorist Persons and Transfer of
       Funds (Information on the Payer) Regulations 2017 (as amended);
     - The Singapore Monetary Authority of Singapore's Notice on
       Prevention of Money- Laundering and Countering the Financing of
       Terrorism (MAS Notice 626); and
     - Equivalent AML/CFT regimes in all other Regulated Jurisdictions.

================================================================================
6. SECURITY AND RISK MANAGEMENT
================================================================================

6.1  Licensee acknowledges that the VaultBank Platform implements
     enterprise-grade security controls consistent with the requirements
     of:

     - The Swiss Financial Market Infrastructure Act (FMIS) and FINMA
       Circular 2018/1 on outsourcing;
     - The Basel Committee on Banking Supervision (BCBS) "Principles
       for Operational Resilience";
     - The NIST Cybersecurity Framework (CSF) 2.0;
     - The ISO/IEC 27001:2022 and ISO/IEC 27002:2022 standards;
     - The Payment Services Directive 2 (PSD2) Strong Customer
       Authentication (SCA) requirements under Regulatory Technical
       Standards (RTS) on strong customer authentication;
     - The PCI DSS Version 4.0 and the PCI Secure Software Framework;
     - The SWIFT Customer Security Programme (CSP) and SWIFT's
       "My Baseline Control Framework" (MBCF);
     - The Cloud Security Alliance (CSA) Security Best Practices; and
     - The OWASP Top 10 and OWASP API Security Top 10 (2023).

6.2  Licensee shall not attempt to circumvent, bypass, or defeat any
     security controls, authentication mechanisms, encryption protocols,
     or access controls implemented within the Software, in accordance
     with Article 8(2) of the EU Cybersecurity Act and equivalent
     provisions under the U.S. Computer Fraud and Abuse Act (CFAA),
     the UK Computer Misuse Act 1990, and the UAE Cybercrime Law
     (Federal Decree-Law No. 5 of 2012).

6.3  The Software incorporates real-time anomaly detection and fraud
     prevention systems powered by the VaultBank "Sentinel" engine,
     which utilises machine learning models trained on synthetic and
     anonymised transaction data in compliance with GDPR Article 89
     (safeguards for processing).

================================================================================
7. TERM AND TERMINATION
================================================================================

7.1  This Agreement commences on the date of first access to the Software
     and continues indefinitely unless terminated in accordance with this
     Section 7.

7.2  Either party may terminate this Agreement immediately upon written
     notice if the other party:

     (a) Becomes insolvent, enters into liquidation, or has a receiver
         or administrator appointed over its assets;
     (b) Materially breaches any provision of this Agreement and fails
         to cure such breach within thirty (30) days of written notice;
     (c) Is found to be acting in contravention of applicable financial
         services, AML/CFT, or sanctions laws; or
     (d) Attempts to reverse engineer, circumvent security controls, or
         unlawfully access VaultBank production systems or customer data.

7.3  Upon termination, Licensee shall immediately cease all use of the
     Software and shall destroy all copies of the Software and
     Confidential Information in its possession, except as required by
     law for audit or compliance purposes.

