10. GOVERNING LAW AND DISPUTE RESOLUTION
================================================================================

10.1 This Agreement shall be governed by and construed in accordance
     with the laws of the Swiss Confederation, without regard to its
     conflict of laws principles. The United Nations Convention on
     Contracts for the International Sale of Goods (CISG) shall not
     apply.

10.2 Any dispute, controversy, or claim arising out of or relating to
     this Agreement, including its existence, validity, interpretation,
     performance, breach, or termination, shall be resolved by binding
     arbitration administered by the Swiss Chambers of Commerce and
     Industry in accordance with its Swiss Rules of International
     Arbitration ("Swiss Rules of Arbitration"), and any arbitral
     proceedings shall be conducted in English in Zurich, Switzerland.

10.3 Notwithstanding the foregoing, each party reserves the right to
     seek injunctive or equitable relief in any court of competent
     jurisdiction to prevent a party from breaching its confidentiality
     obligations or engaging in unlawful activity, including money
     laundering or sanctions violations, without proof of actual
     damages and without bond or other security being required.

10.4 This Agreement is subject to the mandatory provisions of the
     following jurisdictions insofar as such provisions confer
     protections on consumers or data subjects that may not be waived
     by contract:

     (a) The Consumer Rights Act 2015 (UK) and equivalent consumer
         protection laws in the European Economic Area;
     (b) The California Consumer Privacy Act (CCPA) and California
         Civil Code Section 1798.199.90 (right to correct and delete
         personal information), where applicable;
     (c) The UAE Consumer Protection Regulations, Federal Law No. 15
         of 2018, where applicable;
     (d) The Singapore Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act
         (Cap. 52B), where applicable; and
     (e) The Swiss Unfair Competition Act (UCA) (SR 250.005),
         where applicable.

